{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgjNEFnoYL98eLpPg5K9U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Liur5wPVJXxh2qJRCm9DCS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > sec10_conclusion.tex <<'EOF'\n% Conclusion -- drafted by loop0015 item 09 (2026-11-05), in plain English\n% (owner's rule of 2026-11-05 05:30). The second subsection reviews every\n% entry of paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD written up to this section (S1-S8,\n% 01a-08xd, and 09a-09d of this item) and lists the ones that affect the\n% text as open, by entry number; the owner resolves an entry by editing the\n% paper and striking it. Nothing here is a new number: every figure quoted\n% is a later section's, with its section named.\n\\section{Conclusion}\n\\label{sec:conclusion}\n\\begingroup\\sloppy\n\nOpenAI's family 378 holds a theorem the Lean kernel accepts, and the\ntheorem refutes the Exponential Time Hypothesis as stated. We read it,\ninspected its proof, rebuilt the proof from source and re-checked it\nwith a second checker, and found no flaw. That is the first thing this\npaper says, and it is said without qualification. The second thing is\nwhat the title says, and it is a reading of the statement, not of the\nproof. The statement is a guarantee: a machine exists and halts within\na bound. The bound's constants exist and are never computed; the proof\nwrites down at least 257 for the exponent's constant and at least\n28,701 for the leading one (Sections~\\ref{sec:statement} and\n\\ref{sec:proof}). The exponent is the manuscript's weaker one, and with\nits constant set to one it exceeds the number of variables at every\nsize from 50 up to a number with 2,391 digits\n(Section~\\ref{sec:statement}). So at every practical size the verified\nguarantee is weaker than the guarantee of trying every assignment. The\nmanuscript's sharper exponents, which would change that sentence, are\nnot in the Lean library (Section~\\ref{sec:beyond}). What follows from\nthe verified statement is exactly what the manuscript says follows: the\nhypotheses fall, the lower bounds derived from them lose their premise,\nand the conclusions of those lower bounds are untouched\n(Section~\\ref{sec:consequences}). For anyone who runs a solver, nothing\nchanges (Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner}). The two facts are true at\nonce, and neither diminishes the other: in the limit the exponent is\nsmaller than the number of variables by any factor one names, which is\na theorem in our own Lean (Section~\\ref{sec:lean}); on every size anyone\nwill write down, it is larger.\n\n\\subsection{What is claimed, and what is not}\n\\label{sec:conclusion-claims}\n\nThe introduction's two lists (Section~\\ref{sec:intro-claims}) are the\npaper's claims and non-claims, and each later section repeats its own\nunder ``what this does not claim''. In one sentence each: the verified\nstatement is a guarantee with uncomputed constants, above $2^n$ at every\npractical size with the constants set to one, and refuting ETH and its\nrelatives nonetheless; the proof shows no flaw by inspection, builds\nfrom source, and passes two checkers; the sharper exponents are\npaper-only; and no running time of any machine, no flaw in anything,\nno value of any constant beyond the proof's own, and no refutation of\nany derived lower bound's conclusion is asserted. Every number in the\npaper has a script under \\repofile{paper3/scripts/} that regenerates\nit, every quotation has a page and line or a file and line, and the\nreplay's logs and hashes are under \\repofile{paper3/replay/}.\n\n\\subsection{The questions this reading left open, by entry}\n\\label{sec:conclusion-open}\n\nThe paper was written under a rule that no question stops the work: a\nchoice between two sound ways of saying or doing a thing is made,\nrecorded in \\repofile{paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD} as one numbered entry\nwith what was ambiguous, what was chosen and what the author may want\nto change, and the writing goes on. Forty-four entries were written\nbefore this section and four by it. We reviewed all forty-eight and\nsort them here. Fourteen need no decision: six were resolved by the\nauthor in writing (S1, the author line; S3, where the companion Lean\nlives, with 07a following it; S4, no width references; S6, the model\ncounters; S7, the phrase ``for every $50 \\le n < e^{5504}$''; S8, the\nreplay's Lean version) and eight are procedural or are corrections\nalready carried by the text (S5, the per-item time cap of the writing\ndriver; 01a, the sandbox's core cap; 03b, the manuscript has 67 pages;\n04b, 04d and 04e, three counts corrected from an earlier audit; 06b, a\ncounter installed for Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner}; 08xb, which\nsections the plain-English rewrite covered). The thirty-four below\naffect the text and are open: in each case the text stands as chosen,\nand the entry says what would change.\n\n\\begin{description}\\setlength{\\itemsep}{1pt}\n\\item[The title and its figures.] S2: $2^n$ is typeset with a\n  superscript and the ellipsis as three dots; the plain text is in the\n  PDF's metadata. 02a: Section~\\ref{sec:statement} carries both the\n  two-panel Figure~\\ref{fig:central} and Figure~\\ref{fig:runtime-scale},\n  three drawings of one function. 02b: the central figure's peak is\n  placed analytically and its legend carries the $+16$.\n\\item[The statement (Section~\\ref{sec:statement}).] 02c: a proof-side\n  fact, the constant $256 + A_t$, is quoted in the statement section\n  for its value. 02d: the Lean theorem is transcribed as a display, not\n  shown verbatim, because the house build cannot typeset its symbols.\n  08xd: Section~\\ref{sec:statement} says the proof's constant is at\n  least 257 and the exhibited theorem's at least 258, two readings of\n  two lines, both kept.\n\\item[Beyond the statement (Section~\\ref{sec:beyond}).] 03a: a third\n  tag, ``supported'', between verified and paper-only. 03c: what the\n  verified exponent would give through Corollary~1.4's argument is not\n  worked out. 03d: Corollary~1.2 is stated with the verified exponent\n  and tagged supported, not verified.\n\\item[The proof and the replay (Sections~\\ref{sec:proof} and\n  \\ref{sec:replay}).] 01b: the second checker is \\texttt{nanoda\\_lib}\n  at the commit named, with \\texttt{lean4export} at the nearest tag.\n  01c: that checker was run with the three axioms permitted and unused\n  axioms ignored. 01d: ``replayed'' means the build, the axiom output\n  and the second checker, not the comparator run. 04a: thirty-five\n  definitions compared, thirty-three identical, two up to a keyword;\n  the audit's ``33'' is explained, not kept. 04c: the exhibited\n  constants, $A \\ge 258$ and $C \\ge 28{,}701$, are stated with their\n  lines.\n\\item[What follows (Section~\\ref{sec:consequences}).] 05a: the\n  manuscript's list of problems is elided from one quotation, by the\n  paper's scope. 05b: SETH is refuted by reading the statement at each\n  width, and ``SETH implies ETH'' is cited for the record. 05c: the\n  hypotheses' sources are copied from the manuscript's reference list\n  and not re-read. 05d: two paragraphs are ours and not the\n  manuscript's, and say so.\n\\item[For the practitioner (Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner}).] 06a: the\n  two guarantee curves share one scale factor, so that they cross where\n  the statement puts the crossing. 06c: seven references for the tools\n  and the threshold are from memory, with no DOI checked. 06d: the\n  counters are reported at their defaults, including a plateau that\n  looks like a preprocessing budget.\n\\item[Our Lean (Section~\\ref{sec:lean}).] 07b: the axiom audit prints\n  two lines with fewer than the three axioms, and ``every line on the\n  three'' is read as ``nothing beyond the three''. 07c: the re-diff also\n  matches the restatement's body to the theorem's, beyond what was\n  asked.\n\\item[Related work (Section~\\ref{sec:related}).] 08a: the audit paper's\n  title is typeset with an apostrophe the arXiv record lacks. 08b: four\n  small public records were fetched beside the three allowed pages, for\n  their dates and commits. 08c: fourteen references carry no checked\n  DOI. 08d: ``we found no earlier statement'' is bounded to six texts.\n\\item[Plain English, and this section.] 08xa: the dense passages were\n  moved into Appendix~\\ref{app:tech}, not cut. 08xc: the glosses are\n  repeated in each section and now also in the introduction. 09a: the\n  introduction and abstract state the title's third clause in words,\n  with no formula beyond $2^n$, by the plain-English rule rather than\n  by the item's brief. 09b: the abstract carries two numbers, both from\n  Section~\\ref{sec:statement}'s script, and no count from the replay.\n  09c: this sorting of the entries into resolved, procedural and open\n  is the author's to redo. 09d: ``people who checked'' in the stance\n  sentence is read as the author and the assistant the acknowledgements\n  disclose.\n\\end{description}\n\nThirteen of the thirty-four are bibliographic or typographic (S2, 02b,\n02d, 05c, 06c, 08a, 08b, 08c and the five spelling, placement and\ntagging choices of 02a, 03a, 03d, 04a, 08xa); the rest are choices\nabout what the text says, and each is a sentence that can be struck\nwithout touching any number.\n\n\\subsection{What this does not claim}\n\\label{sec:conclusion-not}\n\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item \\textbf{Nothing new.} This section states no fact that a\n  previous section does not state with its source; the numbers in it\n  are Sections~\\ref{sec:statement}, \\ref{sec:proof} and\n  \\ref{sec:replay}'s.\n\\item \\textbf{The list of open questions is complete to the day it was\n  written.} Entries added after it, by the reading of the whole paper\n  that follows this draft, are in the file and not here.\n\\item \\textbf{No question is answered here.} Each entry records a\n  choice and what would change; the author's answer, where there is\n  one, is in the file's ``Owner resolutions'' and in the text.\n\\item \\textbf{No claim about the working group.} The collection says a\n  group of computer scientists will examine the proof\n  (Section~\\ref{sec:related}); nothing of theirs is on record here, and\n  their reading of the proof will carry more weight on the proof than\n  our inspection does.\n\\end{itemize}\n\\par\\endgroup\nEOF\necho written; wc -w sec10_conclusion.tex; cd /home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex && make check 2>&1 | tail -5","description":"Write the conclusion and build the paper with the reference check"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1357,"cache_read_input_tokens":219575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1357,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1cad2094-11ee-40b3-a86f-8ba4c86457ea","uuid":"e6e70b59-7375-45b3-a1c6-d4ee514ea645","timestamp":"2026-11-05T07:14:04.587Z","request_id":"req_011CgjNEFRj2ziz93FNAtUf4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Liur5wPVJXxh2qJRCm9DCS":{"command":"cd /home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex && cat > sec10_conclusion.tex <<'EOF'\n% Conclusion -- drafted by loop0015 item 09 (2026-11-05), in plain English\n% (owner's rule of 2026-11-05 05:30). The second subsection reviews every\n% entry of paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD written up to this section (S1-S8,\n% 01a-08xd, and 09a-09d of this item) and lists the ones that affect the\n% text as open, by entry number; the owner resolves an entry by editing the\n% paper and striking it. Nothing here is a new number: every figure quoted\n% is a later section's, with its section named.\n\\section{Conclusion}\n\\label{sec:conclusion}\n\\begingroup\\sloppy\n\nOpenAI's family 378 holds a theorem the Lean kernel accepts, and the\ntheorem refutes the Exponential Time Hypothesis as stated. We read it,\ninspected its proof, rebuilt the proof from source and re-checked it\nwith a second checker, and found no flaw. That is the first thing this\npaper says, and it is said without qualification. The second thing is\nwhat the title says, and it is a reading of the statement, not of the\nproof. The statement is a guarantee: a machine exists and halts within\na bound. The bound's constants exist and are never computed; the proof\nwrites down at least 257 for the exponent's constant and at least\n28,701 for the leading one (Sections~\\ref{sec:statement} and\n\\ref{sec:proof}). The exponent is the manuscript's weaker one, and with\nits constant set to one it exceeds the number of variables at every\nsize from 50 up to a number with 2,391 digits\n(Section~\\ref{sec:statement}). So at every practical size the verified\nguarantee is weaker than the guarantee of trying every assignment. The\nmanuscript's sharper exponents, which would change that sentence, are\nnot in the Lean library (Section~\\ref{sec:beyond}). What follows from\nthe verified statement is exactly what the manuscript says follows: the\nhypotheses fall, the lower bounds derived from them lose their premise,\nand the conclusions of those lower bounds are untouched\n(Section~\\ref{sec:consequences}). For anyone who runs a solver, nothing\nchanges (Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner}). The two facts are true at\nonce, and neither diminishes the other: in the limit the exponent is\nsmaller than the number of variables by any factor one names, which is\na theorem in our own Lean (Section~\\ref{sec:lean}); on every size anyone\nwill write down, it is larger.\n\n\\subsection{What is claimed, and what is not}\n\\label{sec:conclusion-claims}\n\nThe introduction's two lists (Section~\\ref{sec:intro-claims}) are the\npaper's claims and non-claims, and each later section repeats its own\nunder ``what this does not claim''. In one sentence each: the verified\nstatement is a guarantee with uncomputed constants, above $2^n$ at every\npractical size with the constants set to one, and refuting ETH and its\nrelatives nonetheless; the proof shows no flaw by inspection, builds\nfrom source, and passes two checkers; the sharper exponents are\npaper-only; and no running time of any machine, no flaw in anything,\nno value of any constant beyond the proof's own, and no refutation of\nany derived lower bound's conclusion is asserted. Every number in the\npaper has a script under \\repofile{paper3/scripts/} that regenerates\nit, every quotation has a page and line or a file and line, and the\nreplay's logs and hashes are under \\repofile{paper3/replay/}.\n\n\\subsection{The questions this reading left open, by entry}\n\\label{sec:conclusion-open}\n\nThe paper was written under a rule that no question stops the work: a\nchoice between two sound ways of saying or doing a thing is made,\nrecorded in \\repofile{paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD} as one numbered entry\nwith what was ambiguous, what was chosen and what the author may want\nto change, and the writing goes on. Forty-four entries were written\nbefore this section and four by it. We reviewed all forty-eight and\nsort them here. Fourteen need no decision: six were resolved by the\nauthor in writing (S1, the author line; S3, where the companion Lean\nlives, with 07a following it; S4, no width references; S6, the model\ncounters; S7, the phrase ``for every $50 \\le n < e^{5504}$''; S8, the\nreplay's Lean version) and eight are procedural or are corrections\nalready carried by the text (S5, the per-item time cap of the writing\ndriver; 01a, the sandbox's core cap; 03b, the manuscript has 67 pages;\n04b, 04d and 04e, three counts corrected from an earlier audit; 06b, a\ncounter installed for Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner}; 08xb, which\nsections the plain-English rewrite covered). The thirty-four below\naffect the text and are open: in each case the text stands as chosen,\nand the entry says what would change.\n\n\\begin{description}\\setlength{\\itemsep}{1pt}\n\\item[The title and its figures.] S2: $2^n$ is typeset with a\n  superscript and the ellipsis as three dots; the plain text is in the\n  PDF's metadata. 02a: Section~\\ref{sec:statement} carries both the\n  two-panel Figure~\\ref{fig:central} and Figure~\\ref{fig:runtime-scale},\n  three drawings of one function. 02b: the central figure's peak is\n  placed analytically and its legend carries the $+16$.\n\\item[The statement (Section~\\ref{sec:statement}).] 02c: a proof-side\n  fact, the constant $256 + A_t$, is quoted in the statement section\n  for its value. 02d: the Lean theorem is transcribed as a display, not\n  shown verbatim, because the house build cannot typeset its symbols.\n  08xd: Section~\\ref{sec:statement} says the proof's constant is at\n  least 257 and the exhibited theorem's at least 258, two readings of\n  two lines, both kept.\n\\item[Beyond the statement (Section~\\ref{sec:beyond}).] 03a: a third\n  tag, ``supported'', between verified and paper-only. 03c: what the\n  verified exponent would give through Corollary~1.4's argument is not\n  worked out. 03d: Corollary~1.2 is stated with the verified exponent\n  and tagged supported, not verified.\n\\item[The proof and the replay (Sections~\\ref{sec:proof} and\n  \\ref{sec:replay}).] 01b: the second checker is \\texttt{nanoda\\_lib}\n  at the commit named, with \\texttt{lean4export} at the nearest tag.\n  01c: that checker was run with the three axioms permitted and unused\n  axioms ignored. 01d: ``replayed'' means the build, the axiom output\n  and the second checker, not the comparator run. 04a: thirty-five\n  definitions compared, thirty-three identical, two up to a keyword;\n  the audit's ``33'' is explained, not kept. 04c: the exhibited\n  constants, $A \\ge 258$ and $C \\ge 28{,}701$, are stated with their\n  lines.\n\\item[What follows (Section~\\ref{sec:consequences}).] 05a: the\n  manuscript's list of problems is elided from one quotation, by the\n  paper's scope. 05b: SETH is refuted by reading the statement at each\n  width, and ``SETH implies ETH'' is cited for the record. 05c: the\n  hypotheses' sources are copied from the manuscript's reference list\n  and not re-read. 05d: two paragraphs are ours and not the\n  manuscript's, and say so.\n\\item[For the practitioner (Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner}).] 06a: the\n  two guarantee curves share one scale factor, so that they cross where\n  the statement puts the crossing. 06c: seven references for the tools\n  and the threshold are from memory, with no DOI checked. 06d: the\n  counters are reported at their defaults, including a plateau that\n  looks like a preprocessing budget.\n\\item[Our Lean (Section~\\ref{sec:lean}).] 07b: the axiom audit prints\n  two lines with fewer than the three axioms, and ``every line on the\n  three'' is read as ``nothing beyond the three''. 07c: the re-diff also\n  matches the restatement's body to the theorem's, beyond what was\n  asked.\n\\item[Related work (Section~\\ref{sec:related}).] 08a: the audit paper's\n  title is typeset with an apostrophe the arXiv record lacks. 08b: four\n  small public records were fetched beside the three allowed pages, for\n  their dates and commits. 08c: fourteen references carry no checked\n  DOI. 08d: ``we found no earlier statement'' is bounded to six texts.\n\\item[Plain English, and this section.] 08xa: the dense passages were\n  moved into Appendix~\\ref{app:tech}, not cut. 08xc: the glosses are\n  repeated in each section and now also in the introduction. 09a: the\n  introduction and abstract state the title's third clause in words,\n  with no formula beyond $2^n$, by the plain-English rule rather than\n  by the item's brief. 09b: the abstract carries two numbers, both from\n  Section~\\ref{sec:statement}'s script, and no count from the replay.\n  09c: this sorting of the entries into resolved, procedural and open\n  is the author's to