er runs to decide a"," formula, and a \\emph{model counter} the one that counts its satisfying"," assignments.","-A \\emph{guarantee} is a bound a theorem promises; a \\emph{running time}","-is what a clock measures; the two are compared only with their own kind."," ","+\\subsection{What this paper does}","+\\label{sec:intro-summary}","+","+In one paragraph. The verified statement (Section~\\ref{sec:statement})","+says that for each fixed clause width there exist a finite machine of","+the textbook kind, a Turing machine with several tapes, and five","+positive constants. On every formula of that width the machine halts","+with the exact number of satisfying assignments written on a tape. It","+does so within a bound: a constant, times a power of the input length,","+times two raised to a constant times the exponent. The exponent is","+written out in Section~\\ref{sec:statement}. Its ratio to the number of","+variables rises above one at 50, peaks at about 2.17 near a number with","+24 digits, and falls back below one only past a number with 2,391","+digits. The manuscript claims more than the statement","+(Section~\\ref{sec:beyond}): two sharper exponents; a bound on the size","+of logic circuits that depends on one of them; and a chapter of proofs","+by a technique of its own, tensor contraction. We tag every claim","+verified, supported on paper by the verified statement, or paper-only.","+We inspected the proof (Section~\\ref{sec:proof}): all 3,091 source","+files it depends on. They contain no axiom, no omitted proof, no step","+that trusts a compiled program, and no patch to Mathlib, and the","+statement they prove is the one the comparator posed. We replayed it","+(Section~\\ref{sec:replay}). The 3,091 files built from source in a","+sandbox at the pinned Lean version in 33 minutes; the kernel reported","+the three standard axioms; and nanoda re-checked 95,176 declarations,","+the theorem and everything it depends on, with no error. We say what","+follows (Section~\\ref{sec:consequences}). The statement alone refutes","+ETH, SETH, the gap form, the form for guessing (nondeterministic)","+machines, the counting form, and the randomised forms of ETH, SETH and","+the gap form. A lower bound that was proved \\emph{from} one of them is","+an ``if \\ldots{} then'' whose ``if'' is now false: it derives nothing,","+and the statement it concluded is not itself refuted. We say what it","+changes for a practitioner (Section~\\ref{sec:practitioner}): nothing on","+any machine. We show that by timing an ordinary SAT solver and two model","+counters on random formulas of up to 500 variables and drawing the two","+guarantees beside the measurements. We restate the verified sentence in","+our own Lean library under one name, with its axioms audited","+(Section~\\ref{sec:lean}). And we place the paper beside what the","+collection, the hypotheses' authors, a published human audit, and the","+two checking tools say about themselves (Section~\\ref{sec:related}).","+"," \\subsection{What is claimed, and what is not}"," \\label{sec:intro-claims}"," "]},{"oldStart":135,"oldLines":26,"newStart":145,"newLines":26,"lines":["   (Section~\\ref{sec:statement})."," \\item With every constant set to one, the verified exponent exceeds the","   number of variables at every size from 50 up to a number with 2,391","-  digits, so the verified bound is above $2^n$ there; with the true","-  constants, which are unknown and at least 257 in the proof on record,","-  it is higher still (Section~\\ref{sec:statement}).","-\\item The manuscript's two sharper exponents, and the quantitative","-  circuit bound that rests on one of them, are not in the Lean library","+  digits, so the verified bound is above $2^n$ there. The true constants","+  are unknown and at least 257 in the proof on record, so with them the","+  bound is higher still (Section~\\ref{sec:statement}).","+\\item The manuscript's two sharper exponents, and the circuit bound that","+  rests on one 